        "description": "reconsider groups: {\"g96\":\"This group clusters distinct parties. Merge i2 with i65 as Server-PI, and i5 with i68 as Server-A-PI in the third-party flow; keep i36 Server-FTP separate because the RFC defines that process as including PI and DTP, rather than as the direct control-connection role.\",\"g98\":\"i45 is the RFC959 FTP data connection used by MLSD, not a separate transport channel: RFC3659 says it opens the data connection per RFC959 and applies TYPE L 8, MODE S, STRU F only for this command. Merge it with i10/i73 so endpoints remain server-DTP and user-DTP with the source-defined direction; retain the MLSD parameter settings and lifecycle on its steps.\",\"g99\":\"i15 and i80 are the same FTP reply send operation after party and channel normalization. i27 is a different peer: Server A PI replies to User-PI on the control connection to Server A. Keep i27 separate and reference that server-A-specific channel.\"}",
